  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through Monday)\nIssued at 412 AM EDT Tue Jul 28 2026\n\nGlobal and ensemble solutions show fair agreement in describing \ndrier conditions establishing during much of the long term as the \ndeeper moisture and instability remains over the northern half of \nthe peninsula through the weekend. Latest NBM seems to also embrace \nthe likelihood of having a significant intrusion of a SAL that may \nlast through Saturday. This will result in a reduction in afternoon \nconvection and less cloud coverage each day. \n\nPOPs/Wx coverage drops to 20-40% each afternoon through Friday, \nfavoring the northern-most areas of SoFlo where the better pool \nmoisture will reside. Then for the weekend, a series of short wave \nimpulses will travel along a deepening trough over the E CONUS and \npush some of the lingering moisture over northern Florida back into \nthe area. This will result in increasing coverage with a gradient of \nPOPs south-to-north from 20-30% around Miami-Dade to 55-60% around \nthe Lake region.  \n\nTemperatures will remain above normals, with highs generally in the \nlow to mid 90s, and morning lows in the mid 70s over inland South FL \nto around 80 closer to the coasts.",
